# Never upload local env files to a Vercel build.
#
# This is not only about secrets. A local .env carrying VITE_USE_MOCK=true
# gets read by Vite during the Vercel build, folds `live` to false, and the
# minifier then dead-code-eliminates the entire network branch — producing a
# production bundle that physically cannot call the API and silently serves
# the scripted mock instead. That shipped once (14.8.2026).
#
# Production configuration belongs in the Vercel project environment, never
# in an uploaded file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local build output — Vercel builds server-side.
dist
node_modules
